course: dictionary
lesson: 14915
title: Redouble: trying harder
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Redouble is a verb, and it means to make an effort, a feeling or an action much stronger or greater. The little word «re» at the front is a clue: it means again, so redouble is like doing something again, but even more strongly. «The rescuers heard a cry from the cave, so they redoubled their efforts.» They did not just try again. They tried much harder.
explain: Look at the words around redouble to check your meaning. «Mia was behind in the race, so she redoubled her speed on the last lap.» Mia was losing, so she ran faster at the end. Swap in «tried much harder» and the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Redouble does not usually mean exactly two times. It means a lot more. «Tom had forgotten his spellings, so he redoubled his efforts to learn them.» Tom did not learn twice as many words. He worked a lot harder than before.
explain: Redouble also has a special meaning in the card game bridge, where players make bids. There it means to double a bid that has already been doubled. You will only need this meaning in card games, so for school stories, think of trying harder.
fact: Redouble is a verb. Its forms are redouble, redoubles, redoubled and redoubling.
fact: «Redouble» means to make an effort, a feeling or an action much stronger or greater.
fact: Phrases to know: «redouble your efforts» and «redoubled their search».
fact: The start «re-» often means again, so redouble is like doing something again, but more strongly.
fact: In the card game bridge, redouble means to double again a bid that has already been doubled.
exercise: «The rescuers heard a cry, so they redoubled their efforts.» What does redoubled mean here? | Gave up and went home | Fell asleep | Stopped to eat lunch | *Tried much harder
exercise: Ella had only two days left before her test, so she ___ her practice. What word fits best? | *redoubled | forgot | ended | sneezed
exercise: Which sentence shows the strongest effort? | The rescuers tried a little | The rescuers were bored | The rescuers sat down to rest | *The rescuers redoubled their efforts
test: «The runner was tired, but she redoubled her speed at the end of the race.» What does redoubled mean? | Stopped to sleep | Fell over | *Ran much faster | Slowed down
test: In the card game bridge, what does redouble mean? | To leave the table | To shuffle the cards | *To double again a bid that has already been doubled | To stop playing for the day
exam: Which sentence uses redouble correctly? | The dog redoubled under the table | The sky redoubled because it was sunny | Sam ate a sandwich and redoubled his lunch | *The team redoubled their efforts to win the match
